|> Exercise
    handle=_can_B1B2_be_rewritten_

    True or false: 
    for all $B_1$, $B_2 \in \rr$,
    !! an expression of the form
    $$
    \cos(B_1x) + \sin(B_2x)
    $$
    can be rewritten
    $$
    W\cdot\cos(x + \psi)
    $$
    for some $W$, $\psi \in \rr$.

    |> Solution

        If $B_1 = B_2 = 2$, e.g., then
        $$
        \cos(B_1x) + \sin(B_2x) = \cos(2x) + \sin(2x)
        $$
        is periodic mod $2\eta$, but
        $$
        W\cdot \cos(x + \psi)
        $$
        is only going to be periodic mod $4\eta$, not
        $2\eta$, unless one sets $W = 0$, which is obviously
        not going to work, so the statement is false.
